1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Dear Professor Al-Haddad — the demonstration
you asked for.

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,250
No sound: the captions are the commentary.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,000
First the eight-stage pipeline, then the
Grad-CAM maps.

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:21,260
This is Lite mode — the clinician's screen.
The research view comes later.

5
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:31,510
One patient, both eyes, uploaded as ordinary
files.

6
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,460
EyePACS case 294 - proliferative retinopathy
in both eyes.

7
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:41,010
The system is not told that grade. We compare
against it.

8
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:50,260
Each image is checked to be a fundus
photograph, then a patient case opens on the server.

9
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:58,010
Every stage can now be inspected one by one,
on this eye.

10
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:04,260
The image as it left the camera: a left eye,
disc on the left.

11
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,000
Stage 0 mirrors every left eye into right-eye
orientation.

12
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:16,250
After it, the optic disc sits on the same side
in every image.

13
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,500
A trained heat-map detector finds the optic
disc and the fovea.

14
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:29,250
It reports its confidence and can show its
probability map.

15
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:35,000
A clinician who disagrees drags the markers;
the pipeline re-runs.

16
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:41,260
Stage 1 rotates the disc-to-fovea axis
horizontal.

17
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:45,510
Camera tilt stops being a difference between
images.

18
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:52,460
Stage 2 crops the field of view and resizes to
512 by 512.

19
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:56,510
The resize is isotropic — nothing is
stretched.

20
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:02,750
Stage 3 builds a binary mask of the field of
view.

21
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,500
The mask becomes the fourth input channel of
the network.

22
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:14,750
Stage 4 removes the camera's illumination
gradient.

23
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,500
The dark corners lift; lesions stop competing
with shading.

24
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:27,250
Stage 5 is dual-constraint CLAHE on the
lightness channel.

25
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:32,500
The second constraint keeps the optic disc
from burning out.

26
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:37,750
These two photometric stages carry 41 % of the
measured gain.

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,500
The channels of the final stage are the CNN
input itself.

28
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:48,404
Red, green, blue — and the field-of-view mask.

29
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:55,010
Two stages are absent by design: augmentation
runs only in training,

30
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:59,760
and Stage 7 is the normalisation that produces
the tensor.

31
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
The classifier: EfficientNet-B3, five grades,
four channels.

32
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:15,750
Patient grade, class probabilities, referable
flag, measured latency.

33
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:22,510
Each eye is graded on its own; either eye can
make a patient referable.

34
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:33,750
Grad-CAM, computed live from the model
checkpoint, for each eye.

35
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Attention gathers on the affected periphery,
away from disc and vessels.

36
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:43,250
The line below it is generated from the map
geometry.

37
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:50,000
This is attention alignment, not clinical
localisation of pathology.

38
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:54,250
An interpretability tool, never a diagnostic
output.

39
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:03,000
Here the model's grade matches the dataset's,
and the reviewer confirms it.

40
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:07,750
One verdict per prediction, with an undo.

41
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
A disagreement is recorded the same way, with
the correct grade.

42
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:23,250
It is stored in the patient case and in a
buffer for retraining.

43
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:32,510
The buffer exports as JSONL; the totals are read
from disk, so a disagreement survives a reload.

44
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:40,260
The same page in Full mode: everything behind
the demo.

45
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:48,010
The claim of the work: the model is
preprocessing plus the network.

46
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:53,260
The pipeline is a component of it, not
preparation of the data.

47
00:04:56,510 --> 00:05:01,510
All eight stages, including the two the live
strip cannot show.

48
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:07,262
Stage 6 — affine, colour jitter, noise, JPEG —
training time only.

49
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:12,010
Stage 7 — dataset-specific normalisation into
the tensor.

50
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:20,260
The only change to the backbone is a fourth
channel in the stem.

51
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:25,010
And this is how the attention maps are
produced and scored.

52
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:33,760
Eight datasets: EyePACS for training, the rest
for transfer and external clinics.

53
00:05:37,010 --> 00:05:42,710
Two backbones by two arms, 35,126 images,
five-fold cross-validation.

54
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:48,460
Weighted F1 rises from 0.754 to 0.819 — the
same on both backbones.

55
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:55,010
The arms differ in pipeline and
initialisation, so the gain is the configuration's.

56
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:03,760
Experiment 2 adds the stages one at a time,
under one initialisation.

57
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:09,510
Each contributes significantly; together they
reproduce the whole gain.

58
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:13,390
Flat-field and CLAHE lead — that is the 41 %.

59
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:22,010
The attention claim, measured on 54 IDRiD
images with lesion masks.

60
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:27,760
Overlap rises for all four lesion types; every
interval excludes zero.

61
00:06:31,010 --> 00:06:36,010
Zero-shot transfer to APTOS, then two external
clinical sets.

62
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:40,730
Plus 6.9 points on IDRiD, plus 5.4 on
Messidor-2.

63
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:48,500
Across five camera groups the spread between
devices narrows.

64
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:52,750
On a small clinical set the pipeline still
wins.

65
00:06:56,010 --> 00:07:01,510
The headline metrics, and the tests behind
them: DeLong, McNemar, Holm.

66
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:08,760
The fourth channel costs under 1 % in FLOPs
and 24 megabytes.

67
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:12,510
The pipeline is a cheap prior.

68
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:19,750
The demo is online; I will keep the backend
running to suit you.

69
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,500
Thank you for your time and for your review.
